    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\theta=40^\\circ,\\ 80^\\circ,\\ 160^\\circ$.",
      "worked": "Using the given identity,\n$$\\begin{align*}2(4\\cos^3\\theta-3\\cos\\theta)+1&=0\\\\2\\cos 3\\theta+1&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nLet $u=3\\theta$. Since $\\theta\\in[0^\\circ,180^\\circ]$, $u\\in[0^\\circ,540^\\circ]$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2\\cos u+1&=0\\\\\\cos u&=-\\frac12\\\\u&=120^\\circ,\\ 240^\\circ,\\ 480^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{120^\\circ}{3},\\ \\frac{240^\\circ}{3},\\ \\frac{480^\\circ}{3}\\\\\\theta&=40^\\circ,\\ 80^\\circ,\\ 160^\\circ.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
